</blockquote>
<p>Since SCP-4000-2 items can contain sensitive information, including Foundation-wide used memes and anti-memes that people may not be cleared for, only D-Class subjects inside facilities designed to recognize them and obscure them (the Black Box, albeit I just resigned to not explaining anything about them since this articled had become unwieldy enough by that time), amnesticizing them right after researchers are done with them, may handle the things. MTF Alpha-1 sends specially cleared personnel to collect them. The rest are Safe and store in SSLs, since they are, well, Safe by Box Test standards.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Boy, that's an awful lot of addenda that I just have no idea what the purpose of was. c.c</p>
