<p>Honestly, I was enjoying it up until the interview.</p>
<p>The language, SCP-4000-1, and the SCP-4000-2 instances have wonderful logic to them that really make that part of the article a blast read, and you are rather creative in the kinds of memories and effects the various ripe stones impart. Had you settled there with a kicker entry on the log (kind of like in Tatiana's Prison) I would have upvoted in a heartbeat.</p>
<p>But then we get to the interview, and the piece bogs down in such a massive storm of all caps and exposition that the pacing stops and, at least for me, the reader is left to slog through the rest.</p>
<p>I can appreciate the ambition of this piece, and the theme of the impact of the various X000 articles on the wiki. However, as rumetzen aptly said above, this could have probably gotten the same impact in about half the length.</p>
