			<div class="content" id="post-content-3905820">
									

<p>+1 for the sheer number of moments I enjoyed out of this, although you had me swinging back and forth on it <em>a lot.</em></p>
<p>Regarding things that could be cut, for the big one, there were <em>way</em> too many -2 descriptions and/or too much detail, to the point that (on mobile) I was getting angry just seeing the next one. Seeing D-Class get maimed added next-to-nothing to this, and I never read the stone shape descriptions at all. If there was some special logic for including all the SCP stones you did, it wasn't worth it.</p>
<p>And then so many reacted/contentless ones? No.</p>
<p>Besides that&#8230; I guess the mother's speech.was very ostentatious and slightly repetitive, so that part could be trimmed. Clio could probably be shortened up. Maybe in the language about the timelines, or her and her mother's past. Again, maybe look for repetition between statements or extra flourish that doesn't add much? Sorry I don't have as much direct advice here, unlike the -2s.</p>
<p>Edit: specifically look for where you've told the same story or parts of the same story twice? Without looking back, I feel like that happens a lot. Edit edit: Or times when a character is protesting something repeatedly.</p>
<p>SCP-2000 being an ancient vault thing was something I didn't like. That's not a cutting suggestion, just registering my opinion.</p>

